  "reference-examples-p0-expansion-2026-07-16.jsonl carries exactly
   137 × 2 = 274 dedup-per-verb pairs.")

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; COVERAGE IMPACT
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

(coverage-impact
  :measurement-note
  "Coverage tiers per architect-plan: STARVED (0 pairs), THIN (1-4),
   THIN-CONTEXT (5-19 OR <3 books), HEALTHY (>=20 AND >=3 books).
   Reference-example-extractor measures reference-only pairs. Every P0
   target verb had 3 pairs pre-injection (from the reference's baseline
   3-tier examples) and now has 5+ from the reference alone."

  :pre-injection
  ((:tier "STARVED (0 ref pairs)"  :count 0 :note "Reference already had 3 examples per verb")
   (:tier "THIN (1-4 ref pairs)"   :count 137 :note "All P0 targets were at 3")
   (:tier "THIN-CONTEXT (5-19)"    :count 0)
   (:tier "HEALTHY (>=20)"         :count 0))

  :post-injection
  ((:tier "STARVED (0 ref pairs)"  :count 0)
   (:tier "THIN (1-4 ref pairs)"   :count 0 :note "All P0 targets promoted out of THIN")
   (:tier "THIN-CONTEXT (5-19)"    :count 137 :note "All targets at 5+")
   (:tier "HEALTHY (>=20)"         :count 0 :note "HEALTHY needs book-chapter contexts too — P0 authoring only touched the reference"))

  :promotion-summary
  "137 of 137 P0 targets moved from THIN (3 pairs) to THIN-CONTEXT (5 pairs).
   HEALTHY promotion requires additional book-chapter authoring (P0
   scope covered reference only; book-chapter demos are the P1/P2 pass
   per Plan A structure)."

  :whole-corpus-tier-distribution
  ((:pairs-per-verb 3 :verbs 771)
   (:pairs-per-verb 5 :verbs 134)
   (:pairs-per-verb 6 :verbs 13)
   (:pairs-per-verb 7 :verbs 2)
   (:pairs-per-verb 8 :verbs 28)
   (:pairs-per-verb 10 :verbs 1)
   :note "771 verbs still at baseline 3 (waiting on P1+P2). 134 at 5
    are P0-targets. 28 at 8 were already-lifted before P0 (had 5 in-ref
    examples). 13 at 6 are duplicate-name records that accumulated
    across two entries. 2 at 7 and 1 at 10 are duplicate-name records
    that received the P0 injection twice."))

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; SAMPLE PAIRS (3 from the delta JSONL)
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

(sample-pairs
  (:sample-1
   :verb "ai/arrive"
   :batch "B-03"
   :tier "novice"
   :user "Write a novice Motoi example that uses `ai/arrive`."
   :assistant "```motoi\n(ai/arrive 'hero 100 100)\n```\n\nSteer the hero to (100, 100). Slows down as it gets close so it doesn't overshoot.")

  (:sample-2
   :verb "grid-step-count"
   :batch "B-01"
   :tier "novice"
   :user "Write a novice Motoi example that uses `grid-step-count`."
   :assistant "```motoi\n(display (grid-step-count))\n```\n\nHow many steps has the grid taken since it was initialized?")

  (:sample-3
   :verb "entity/apply-force!"
   :batch "B-02"
   :tier "intermediate"
   :user "Show me `entity/apply-force!` at the intermediate level."
   :assistant "```motoi\n(on-key\n  (lambda (k)\n    (when (eq? k 'up)\n      (entity/apply-force! 'hero 0 -12))))\n```\n\nUp arrow gives the hero an upward impulse. Multiple presses stack — the force is additive."))

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; BLOCKERS / OPEN QUESTIONS
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

(blockers-open-questions
  (:item "plan-target-count-mismatch"
   :severity :LOW
   :description
   "Plan quotes 86 STARVED verbs for B-01; empirical scan of core
    library against the plan's prefix set yielded 76 (some plan-listed
    prefixes like extras beyond the enumerated ones did not surface).
    Total P0 executed = 137 verbs, not 147. The 10-verb gap is in
    B-01 only; other batches match plan counts exactly."
   :next-step "Architect to reconcile plan's 86 target vs empirical 76.")

  (:item "starved-vs-thin-baseline"
   :severity :LOW
   :description
   "Plan describes STARVED targets as '0-2 examples'. Empirical scan of
    the reference on 2026-07-16 shows EVERY targeted verb already had 3
    examples (the reference's baseline). Plan A P0 therefore lifted
    3 → 5, not 0-2 → 5. Coverage improvement is real but smaller per
    verb than the plan's yield estimate."
   :next-step "Delta JSONL reports actual +274 pairs from 137 verbs.")

  (:item "healthy-tier-promotion"
   :severity :MEDIUM
   :description
   "HEALTHY tier requires >=20 pairs AND >=3 books per plan. Reference-
    only edits reach 5 pairs and 1 book (the reference itself). Book-
    chapter authoring (the second half of Plan A per verb) is out of
    scope for this P0 execution — required to hit HEALTHY."
   :next-step "P1 or subsequent lane: author fenced ```motoi``` blocks in
    the book-chapter hosts listed per batch in the plan.")

  (:item "no-ambiguous-verbs"
   :severity :NONE
   :description
   "No P0 target verb required :needs-alfred tagging. Every signature
    and summary in the reference gave enough context for safe example
    authoring. No fabrication was necessary.")

  (:item "extractor-audit-clean"
   :severity :NONE
   :description
   "Post-injection extractor run: 962 verb records scanned, 949 unique,
    0 malformed forms, 0 empty codes, 0 unavailable codes. Paren
    balance verified: final depth = 0."))

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; METHOD NOTES (for the next batch runner)
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

(method-notes
  :ordering
  "Each verb kept its existing 3 examples [novice, intermediate, expert].
   Two new examples appended: 1 novice + 1 intermediate. Final tier
   distribution per verb: [novice, intermediate, expert, novice,
   intermediate] = 2 novice + 2 intermediate + 1 expert, matching the
   Plan A spec."

  :safety
  ("Reference backed up first to .bak-2026-07-16-p0-execution before
    any edit."
   "Injector idempotent-detects: if new code already exists inside the
    verb's :examples body, that example is skipped. 13 skipped on first
    run; 13 fresh novice codes authored to avoid collisions on second
    run."
   "Paren balance verified post-injection."
   "Every verb form in the reference remains structurally intact —
    only the :examples list body was extended.")

  :extractor-yield-per-verb
  "Each new example -> 1 JSONL pair via the existing reference-example-
   extractor.py. No changes to the extractor were required. Templates
   rotate to avoid same-shape-twice per MEMORY.md sparse-text-abduction
   doctrine."

  :hard-rule-compliance
  ("NO fabrication — every code snippet uses verbs actually documented
    in MOTOI-SCHEME-REFERENCE.slat. No Sakura verbs (card/*, shop/*,
    etc). No philosopher name-drops. No corporate names."
   "Publishable prose in every :note — kid-readable, short, concrete,
    Sakura's teaching voice. No training-data smell."
   "Backup preserved."
   "No git commits."))

